export const EVICTIONS_CARE_NOTE =
  'Teaching, not legal advice, and in this course that warning carries more weight than in any other in the department. What notice a tenant is owed, how long it must run, what a court requires before anybody may be removed, what counts as uninhabitable, and what a landlord is forbidden to do are specific to your state and they change. Changing the locks, shutting off the heat or the water, removing a door, or putting somebody’s belongings on the pavement is lawless before Yahweh and is a crime in most places, whatever the tenant has done and whatever you are owed. Get somebody licensed in your own state before you act. If you are the one behind on rent and frightened, start at lesson three and lesson eight — those two are about what may not be done to you, and about what an honest person on the other side is supposed to give back. Nothing here is a substitute for real counsel about your actual situation.';

