      'You find the pronoun, and it is direct — ye cast out, second person, addressed to His own people, with no passive voice to stand behind.',
      'You get the adjective most readers skim past: PLEASANT houses. Not adequate, not sufficient. Somebody liked living there, and the charge names that as part of what was taken.',
