        'Establish first that the law does NOT question the lender’s right to ask for a pledge. Half the misuse of this passage starts from assuming it abolishes the claim.',
        'Verse 10 is the prohibition: he does not cross the door. Not when he is owed, not when he is right, not when the borrower has dragged it out.',
