      howToRun: 'Read the parable through once without stopping. Then go back and build it in three moves: the lawful remedy, the plea and the release that exceeded it, and the turn at verse 28. Before reading verse 29, tell the room to listen carefully to what the fellowservant says — then read 29, then read 26 again, and say nothing at all for a moment. Let somebody in the room name it. Hold the limit yourself, out loud, before anyone applies it to a real situation, and set it explicitly beside last week’s lesson on honouring the end of a window so the two are not heard as contradicting each other.',
